    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nūbae</span></b> , ārum,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νοῦβαι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Africa, to
				the south of Egypt, the Nubians</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
			269</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7,
			664</span></i>.—Also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nūbei</span></b> , ōrum, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 30,
				35, § 192</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A people of Arabia and Syria</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 28,
				32, § 142</span></i>. —In sing.:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nūba</span></b> ,
			ae, <i><span class="en">Claud. Stil. 1,
			252</span></i>.</div>
